# `Gal(κ⟮ζ⟯/κ) ≅ ℤ/ord_n(q)` for a primitive `n`-th root of unity, `p ∤ n`

For a number field `K`, a finite place `𝔭`, `κ = K_𝔭` its `𝔭`-adic completion, `q = residueCard K 𝔭`
the residue field cardinality, and `n` prime to the residue characteristic `p`, the cyclotomic
extension `κ⟮ζ⟯` generated by a primitive `n`-th root of unity is unramified of degree `ord_n(q)`
(with `ord_n(q)` the multiplicative order of `q` modulo `n`), so its `κ`-automorphism group is
cyclic of order `ord_n(q)`:

  `Gal(κ⟮ζ⟯/κ) ≃* Multiplicative (ZMod (ord_n(q)))`.

The isomorphism is non-canonical, hence the statement is `Nonempty`.

The Frobenius — the element of `Gal(κ⟮ζ⟯/κ)` acting as `ζ ↦ ζ ^ q` — is produced from the *global*
cyclotomic field `L = K(ζ_n)`: the global Frobenius at a place `Q ∣ 𝔭` is transported to the
completion `L_Q` (`Submission.NeukirchUchida.Local.decompositionToLocalGalois`), acts on the
residue field by `x ↦ x ^ q` and hence on `ζ_n` by `ζ_n ↦ ζ_n ^ a` with `a ≡ q (mod n)`; its
restriction to the local cyclotomic subfield `κ⟮ζ'⟯ ⊆ L_Q` is the Frobenius.  The degree input is
`NK.TameStructureDeep.Degree.finrank_adjoin_eq_orderOf`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.TameStructureDeep.Degree.Equality
import Submission.NK.TameStructureDeep.Degree.natDegree_minpoly_le_orderOf
import Submission.NK.TameStructureDeep.Units.residueUnits_quot_principalUnits_mulEquiv
import Submission.NK.LocalStructure.Main
